ing a shadow Git repository (no writes to your real repository)"},"50":{"id":"/checkpoint-12","page_id":"/checkpoint","type":"text","url":"/checkpoint#how-checkpoints-work","content":"Example: while developing a feature, the assistant updates multiple files. Each change creates a checkpoint. You can review each modification, and if needed, roll back to any point without impacting your main branch or real Git history."},"51":{"id":"/checkpoint-13","page_id":"/checkpoint","type":"text","url":"/checkpoint#viewing-changes-and-restoring","content":"After each key action, you can:"},"52":{"id":"/checkpoint-14","page_id":"/checkpoint","type":"text","url":"/checkpoint#viewing-changes-and-restoring","content":"Click Compare to see modified files and diffs"},"53":{"id":"/checkpoint-15","page_id":"/checkpoint","type":"text","url":"/checkpoint#viewing-changes-and-restoring","content":"Click Restore to open restore options"},"54":{"id":"/checkpoint-16","page_id":"/checkpoint","type":"text","url":"/checkpoint#restore-options","content":"To go back to a previous point:"},"55":{"id":"/checkpoint-17","page_id":"/checkpoint","type":"text","url":"/checkpoint#restore-options","content":"Click Restore next to any step"},"56":{"id":"/checkpoint-18","page_id":"/checkpoint","type":"text","url":"/checkpoint#restore-options","content":"Choose how you want to restore:"},"57":{"id":"/checkpoint-19","page_id":"/checkpoint","type":"text","url":"/checkpoint#restore-options","content":"Restore Workspace and Task (when available): revert both code and task context"},"58":{"id":"/checkpoint-20","page_id":"/checkpoint","type":"text","url":"/checkpoint#restore-options","content":"Restore Task Only (when available): keep code changes, revert task context"},"59":{"id":"/checkpoint-21","page_id":"/checkpoint","type":"text","url":"/checkpoint#restore-options","content":"Restore Workspace Only: revert code while preserving task context (current default)"},"60":{"id":"/checkpoint-22","page_id":"/checkpoint","type":"text","url":"/checkpoint#restore-options","content":"Note: The current version focuses on “Restore Workspace Only.” Other options will appear as their capabilities are enabled."},"61":{"id":"/checkpoint-23","page_id":"/checkpoint","type":"text","url":"/checkpoint#under-the-hood","content":"In VS Code, Pochi implements checkpoints with a shadow Git that stays separate from your real repository:"},"62":{"id":"/checkpoint-24","page_id":"/checkpoint","type":"text","url":"/checkpoint#under-the-hood","content":"Initializes a bare repository under the extension’s storage directory (scoped per workspace)"},"63":{"id":"/checkpoint-25","page_id":"/checkpoint","type":"text","url":"/checkpoint#under-the-hood","content":"Points the worktree to your workspace, then stages and commits changes into the shadow repo"},"64":{"id":"/checkpoint-26","page_id":"/checkpoint","type":"text","url":"/checkpoint#under-the-hood","content":"Excludes common large/binary/cache/build artifacts (see Exclusions) to keep things fast and stable"},"65":{"id":"/checkpoint-27","page_id":"/checkpoint","type":"text","url":"/checkpoint#under-the-hood","content":"This shadow repo is fully independent. Saving or restoring checkpoints does not create commits in your actual Git repository."},"66":{"id":"/checkpoint-28","page_id":"/checkpoint","type":"text","url":"/checkpoint#requirements","content":"Git must be installed (the shadow Git depends on it). If Git isn’t available, the checkpoint feature can’t initialize and will be disabled."},"67":{"id":"/checkpoint-29","page_id":"/checkpoint","type":"text","url":"/checkpoint#smart-detection-and-exclusions","content":"Pochi automatically detects and excludes heavy or redundant files to keep checkpoints lean and fast, including:"},"68":{"id":"/checkpoint-30","page_id":"/checkpoint","type":"text","url":"/checkpoint#smart-detection-and-exclusions","content":"Build artifacts and dependency folders"},"69":{"id":"/checkpoint-31","page_id":"/checkpoint","type":"tex