oes. This is used to help Pochi decide when to use your agent."},"117":{"id":"/custom-agent-20","page_id":"/custom-agent","type":"text","url":"/custom-agent#configuration","content":"tools (optional): A list of tools that the agent is allowed to use. This can be a comma-separated string (e.g., tool-1, tool-2) or a YAML array. If omitted, the agent inherits all available tools."},"118":{"id":"/custom-agent-21","page_id":"/custom-agent","type":"text","url":"/custom-agent#tool-specific-rules","content":"Rule entries follow the format tool or tool(specifier). The following tools support specifier-based restrictions:"},"119":{"id":"/custom-agent-22","page_id":"/custom-agent","type":"text","url":"/custom-agent#tool-specific-rules","content":"executeCommand — Command patterns, e.g. executeCommand(npm run *)"},"120":{"id":"/custom-agent-23","page_id":"/custom-agent","type":"text","url":"/custom-agent#tool-specific-rules","content":"readFile, writeToFile, applyDiff, editNotebook — Path globs, e.g. readFile(src/**)"},"121":{"id":"/custom-agent-24","page_id":"/custom-agent","type":"text","url":"/custom-agent#tool-specific-rules","content":"webFetch — Domain patterns, e.g. webFetch(domain:*.example.com)"},"122":{"id":"/custom-agent-25","page_id":"/custom-agent","type":"text","url":"/custom-agent#tool-specific-rules","content":"A tool declared without parentheses (e.g., readFile) has no restrictions. Use one declaration per rule — commas inside a specifier are not supported; add separate entries for multiple rules."},"123":{"id":"/custom-agent-26","page_id":"/custom-agent","type":"text","url":"/custom-agent#command-execution-restrictions","content":"Restrict which shell commands the agent can run via executeCommand. The specifier is matched against each individual command segment (split on ;, &&, ||, |). If any segment does not match at least one allowed pattern, the tool call is rejected."},"124":{"id":"/custom-agent-27","page_id":"/custom-agent","type":"text","url":"/custom-ag