ras"},"241":{"id":"/models-6","page_id":"/models","type":"heading","url":"/models#deepinfra","content":"DeepInfra"},"242":{"id":"/models-7","page_id":"/models","type":"heading","url":"/models#groq","content":"Groq"},"243":{"id":"/models-8","page_id":"/models","type":"heading","url":"/models#lm-studio","content":"LM Studio"},"244":{"id":"/models-9","page_id":"/models","type":"heading","url":"/models#mistral","content":"Mistral"},"245":{"id":"/models-10","page_id":"/models","type":"heading","url":"/models#ollama","content":"Ollama"},"246":{"id":"/models-11","page_id":"/models","type":"text","url":"/models#models","content":"Pochi leverages the AI SDK to support various LLM providers and can run local models."},"247":{"id":"/models-12","page_id":"/models","type":"text","url":"/models#pochi","content":"After signing in, you gain access to the Pochi models shown below. Pochi uses a usage-based pricing strategy with no additional charges. For detailed pricing information, visit https://app.getpochi.com/pricing."},"248":{"id":"/models-13","page_id":"/models","type":"text","url":"/models#openai-compatible","content":"Pochi allows you to configure any LLM provider that offers an OpenAI-compatible API by setting up the appropriate API keys. To configure custom models, use the VS Code command Pochi: Open Custom Model Settings to open the settings configuration file."},"249":{"id":"/models-14","page_id":"/models","type":"text","url":"/models#chutes","content":"Chutes provides access to various AI models through their API. To use Chutes, you'll need to obtain an API token from Chutes Platform."},"250":{"id":"/models-15","page_id":"/models","type":"text","url":"/models#cerebras","content":"Cerebras provides AI models through their OpenAI-compatible API. To use Cerebras, you'll need to obtain an API key from Cerebras Platform."},"251":{"id":"/models-16","page_id":"/models","type":"text","url":"/models#deepinfra","content":"DeepInfra provides access to a wide range of AI models through their OpenAI-compatible API. To use DeepInfra, you'll need to obtain an API token from DeepInfra Platform."},"252":{"id":"/models-17","page_id":"/models","type":"text","url":"/models#groq","content":"Groq is a cloud-based AI platform that provides fast inference for large language models."},"253":{"id":"/models-18","page_id":"/models","type":"text","url":"/models#lm-studio","content":"LM Studio is a local IDE application that allows you to run and experiment with language models on your own machine."},"254":{"id":"/models-19","page_id":"/models","type":"text","url":"/models#mistral","content":"Mistral AI provides a range of powerful language models available through their API. To use Mistral models, you'll need to obtain an API key from Mistral AI Platform."},"255":{"id":"/models-20","page_id":"/models","type":"text","url":"/models#ollama","content":"Ollama is a tool that allows you to run large language models locally on your machine with a simple API."},"256":{"id":"/parallel-agents","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"page","content":"Parallel Agents","url":"/parallel-agents"},"257":{"id":"/parallel-agents-0","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"text","url":"/parallel-agents","content":"Run multiple AI agents concurrently to accelerate development and tackle complex tasks."},"258":{"id":"/parallel-agents-1","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"heading","url":"/parallel-agents#parallel-agents","content":"Parallel Agents"},"259":{"id":"/parallel-agents-2","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"heading","url":"/parallel-agents#demo-and-real-world-use-cases","content":"Demo and Real World Use Cases"},"260":{"id":"/parallel-agents-3","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"heading","url":"/parallel-agents#creating-worktree","content":"Creating Worktree"},"261":{"id":"/parallel-agents-4","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"heading","url":"/parallel-agents#create-task-in-pochi","content":"Create Task in Pochi"},"262":{"id":"/parallel-agents-5","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"heading","url":"/parallel-agents#interaction-with-tasks","content":"Interaction with Tasks"},"263":{"id":"/parallel-agents-6","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"text","url":"/parallel-agents#parallel-agents","content":"Most coding assistants can handle one task at a time. But real projects often need multiple agents exploring, refactoring, and developing different features in parallel - across different branches or experiments.\nThat's why we built Parallel Agents."},"264":{"id":"/parallel-agents-7","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"text","url":"/parallel-agents#parallel-agents","content":"Parallel Agents let you run multiple Pochi agents concurrently, each inside its own Git worktree - isolated but synchronized with the same repository.\nEach agent can explore the code base, develop different PRs, or test different ideas in parallel without interfering with each other, while you can check their works and manage them in Pochi extensions."},"265":{"id":"/parallel-agents-8","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"text","url":"/parallel-agents#parallel-agents","content":"Pochi Parallel Agents has the following features:"},"266":{"id":"/parallel-agents-9","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"text","url":"/parallel-agents#parallel-agents","content":"Worktree Integration: Leverage the Git worktree feature to gain an isolated env, did not recreate the wheel again."},"267":{"id":"/parallel-agents-10","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"text","url":"/parallel-agents#parallel-agents","content":"Multi-to-Multi Execution:  Tasks from Pochi could run in different worktree or the same one."},"268":{"id":"/parallel-agents-11","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"text","url":"/parallel-agents#parallel-agents","content":"Task Management: All tasks can be managed on the Pochi sidebar."},"269":{"id":"/parallel-agents-12","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"text","url":"/parallel-agents#parallel-agents","content":"Integrated UX: Review agents' works and open the terminal from one click."},"270":{"id":"/parallel-agents-13","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"text","url":"/parallel-agents#parallel-agents","content":"VSCode Native: Create new Agents directly from the Repository manage view from VSCode."},"271":{"id":"/parallel-agents-14","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"text","url":"/parallel-agents#demo-and-real-world-use-cases","content":"Let's go through the features of Parallel Agents by showing the real world workflow while we are developing Pochi.\nFor the following demo, we will work on those two issues:"},"272":{"id":"/parallel-agents-15","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"text","url":"/parallel-agents#demo-and-real-world-use-cases","content":"https://github.com/TabbyML/pochi/issues/619"},"273":{"id":"/parallel-agents-16","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"text","url":"/parallel-agents#demo-and-real-world-use-cases","content":"https://github.com/TabbyML/pochi/issues/654"},"274":{"id":"/parallel-agents-17","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"text","url":"/parallel-agents#demo-and-real-world-use-cases","content":"Meanwhile, we'll explore together how worktree feature is implemented."},"275":{"id":"/parallel-agents-18","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"text","url":"/parallel-agents#demo-and-real-world-use-cases","content":"We could operate on the default worktree directly; however, since those two issues are independent, we prefer to create a separate worktree for each."},"276":{"id":"/parallel-agents-19","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"text","url":"/parallel-agents#creating-worktree","content":"There are multiple ways to create a new Worktree,"},"277":{"id":"/parallel-agents-20","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"text","url":"/parallel-agents#creating-worktree","content":"Create from Pochi sidebar directly"},"278":{"id":"/parallel-agents-21","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"text","url":"/parallel-agents#creating-worktree","content":"Create from VSCode Repository management\nYou can first create a new worktree in VSCode Source Control Panel. Then manually link this worktree to a branch, and open this worktree in Pochi."},"279":{"id":"/parallel-agents-22","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"text","url":"/parallel-agents#creating-worktree","content":"Let Pochi create a worktree for a new coding taskWhen you are submitting the message to create a new task, using Cmd/Ctrl + Enter, then Pochi will create a worktree for the new task. The worktree/branch name is generated according to the coding task."},"280":{"id":"/parallel-agents-23","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"text","url":"/parallel-agents#creating-worktree","content":"In all cases, Pochi will create and check out the branch at the specified disk path as a worktree. You can then perform any action as if it were a standard Git repository, as an independent dev environment in each worktree."},"281":{"id":"/parallel-agents-24","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"text","url":"/parallel-agents#create-task-in-pochi","content":"Now we are ready to initiate tasks in each worktree to let them run in parallel. You'd see that once a task is initiated, Pochi opens a new tab for each task, and you can switch between different tabs to monitor the progress of each task."},"282":{"id":"/parallel-agents-25","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"text","url":"/parallel-agents#interaction-with-tasks","content":"When you click on the task, Pochi will open the specific task, allowing you to interact with it."},"283":{"id":"/parallel-agents-26","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"text","url":"/parallel-agents#interaction-with-tasks","content":"For instance, the task fix-issue-654 is now complete. We can review the modifications by selecting Diff worktree with origin/main, and Pochi will open a tab showing all the files changes."},"284":{"id":"/parallel-agents-27","page_id":"/parallel-agents","type":"text","url":"/parallel-agents#interaction-with-tasks","content":"Or choose Open in Integrated Terminal to launch the terminal within this worktree for command execution."},"285":{"id":"/permissions","page_id":"/permissions","type":"page","content":"Permissions","url":"/permissions"},"286":{"id":"/permissions-0","page_id":"/permissions","type":"text","url":"/permissions","content":"Manage Pochi's auto-approval settings"},"287":{"id":"/permissions-1","page_id":"/permissions","type":"heading","url":"/permissions#permissions","content":"Permissions"},"288":{"id":"/permissions-2","page_id":"/permissions","type":"text","url":"/permissions#permissions","content":"By default, all permissions in Pochi are enabled. You can customize these permissions at any time using the Auto-Approve settings."},"289":{"id":"/permissions-3","page_id":"/permissions","type":"text","url":"/permissions#permissions","content":"Read: Read the file content Pochi decides to look up for analyzing or completing tasks."},"290":{"id":"/permissions-4","page_id":"/permissions","type":"text","url":"/permissions#permissions","content":"Write: Creates new files, edits existing code, generates boilerplate, and writes documentation."},"291":{"id":"/permissions-5","page_id":"/permissions","type":"text","url":"/permissions#permissions","content":"Execute: Manages dependencies, runs builds, tests, and perform system operations."},"292":{"id":"/permissions-6","page_id":"/permissions","type":"text","url":"/permissions#permissions","content":"Use MCP: Interacts with databases, APIs, and other external services to expand its capabilities with MCP server."},"293":{"id":"/permissions-7","page_id":"/permissions","type":"text","url":"/permissions#permissions","content":"Retry: Automatically retries failed commands, code changes, and installations."},"294":{"id":"/queued-messages","page_id":"/queued-messages","type":"page","content":"Queued Messages","url":"/queued-messages"},"295":{"id":"/queued-messages-0","page_id":"/queued-messages","type":"text","url":"/queued-messages","content":"Add tasks to a queue while Pochi is busy, ensuring a non-blocking experience."},"296":{"id":"/queued-messages-1","page_id":"/queued-messages","type":"heading","url":"/queued-messages#queued-messages","content":"Queued Messages"},"297":{"id":"/queued-messages-2","page_id":"/queued-messages","type":"text","url":"/queued-messages#queued-messages","content":"The Queued Messages feature allows you to add multiple messages to a queue, which are then combined into a single prompt for execution. This lets you build up a complex request in pieces, which is especially useful while Pochi is busy."},"298":{"id":"/queued-messages-3","page_id":"/queued-messages","type":"text","url":"/queued-messages#queued-messages","content":"When Pochi is busy, you don't have to wait to give it your next instruction. Here’s what happens:"},"299":{"id":"/queued-messages-4","page_id":"/queued-messages","type":"text","url":"/queued-messages#queued-messages","content":"Queue with a Shortcut: Type your prompt and press Cmd+Enter (Ctrl+Enter on Windows/Linux). Your message will be added directly to the queue."},"300":{"id":"/queued-messages-5","page_id":"/queued-messages","type":"text","url":"/queued-messages#queued-messages","content":"See What's in Line: The \"Queued Messages\" panel appears, showing you a list of all the tasks waiting to be executed."},"301":{"id":"/queued-messages-6","page_id":"/queued-messages","type":"text","url":"/queued-messages#queued-messages","content":"Combined for Execution: Once Pochi is ready, it will take all the messages from the queue, merge them into a single prompt, and then execute it."},"302":{"id":"/queued-messages-7","page_id":"/queued-messages","type":"text","url":"/queued-messages#queued-messages","content":"Remove with a Click: If you decide you don't need a task done anymore, just click the X next to it to remove it from the queue."},"303":{"id":"/reviews","page_id":"/reviews","type":"page","content":"Reviews","url":"/reviews"},"304":{"id":"/reviews-0","page_id":"/reviews","type":"text","url":"/reviews","content":"Add, view, and manage line-level comments directly on the diff code"},"305":{"id":"/reviews-1","page_id":"/reviews","type":"heading","url":"/reviews#reviews","content":"Reviews"},"306":{"id":"/reviews-2","page_id":"/reviews","type":"heading","url":"/reviews#how-to-use-reviews","content":"How to Use Reviews"},"307":{"id":"/reviews-3","page_id":"/reviews","type":"heading","url":"/reviews#1-run-a-prompt","content":"1. Run a Prompt"},"308":{"id":"/reviews-4","page_id":"/reviews","type":"heading","url":"/reviews#2-open-the-diff","content":"2. Open the Diff"},"309":{"id":"/reviews-5","page_id":"/reviews","type":"heading","url":"/reviews#3-leave-feedback","content":"3. Leave Feedback"},"310":{"id":"/reviews-6","page_id":"/reviews","type":"heading","url":"/reviews#4-add-multiple-comments","content":"4. Add Multiple Comments"},"311":{"id":"/reviews-7","page_id":"/reviews","type":"heading","url":"/reviews#5-send-comments-as-a-batch","content":"5. Send Comments as a Batch"},"312":{"id":"/reviews-8","page_id":"/reviews","type":"text","url":"/reviews#reviews","content":"Reviews let you leave inline comments directly on the code generated by Pochi inside VS Code. Instead of re-explaining issues in chat, you can comment on specific lines in the diff, batch those comments, and send them back to Pochi for the right contextual fixes."},"313":{"id":"/reviews-9","page_id":"/reviews","type":"text","url":"/reviews#reviews","content":"This feature is not your regular PR review system. It’s actual conversations with the LLM, attached to the code they refer to."},"314":{"id":"/reviews-10","page_id":"/reviews","type":"text","url":"/reviews#reviews","content":"Your browser does not support the video tag."},"315":{"id":"/reviews-11","page_id":"/reviews","type":"text","url":"/reviews#1-run-a-prompt","content":"Generate code or request changes like normal."},"316":{"id":"/reviews-12","page_id":"/reviews","type":"text","url":"/reviews#2-open-the-diff","content":"Once Pochi applies changes, open the diff view in VS Code:"},"317":{"id":"/reviews-13","page_id":"/reviews","type":"text","url":"/reviews#2-open-the-diff","content":"In the diff, hover over a code line and click + to add a comment"},"318":{"id":"/reviews-14","page_id":"/reviews","type":"text","url":"/reviews#3-leave-feedback","content":"Type your comment directly on the line where the issue exists."},"319":{"id":"/reviews-15","page_id":"/reviews","type":"text","url":"/reviews#4-add-multiple-comments","content":"Leave comments across the file as needed. Each comment is automatically linked to its exact line + file path."},"320":{"id":"/reviews-16","page_id":"/reviews","type":"text","url":"/reviews#5-send-comments-as-a-batch","content":"Once you’re done adding comments, submit them just like you would for any other review."},"321":{"id":"/reviews-17","page_id":"/reviews","type":"text","url":"/reviews#5-send-comments-as-a-batch","content":"Click Submit Reviews to Pochi to send all line-level comments as a batch."},"322":{"id":"/reviews-18","page_id":"/reviews","type":"text","url":"/reviews#5-send-comments-as-a-batch","content":"This works the same way as submitting a review with empty messages, where the comments themselves are the request."},"323":{"id":"/reviews-19","page_id":"/reviews","type":"text","url":"/reviews#5-send-comments-as-a-batch","content":"If you want to add extra instructions or context, you can type an additional message in the chat box before submitting."},"324":{"id":"/reviews-20","page_id":"/reviews","type":"text","url":"/reviews#5-send-comments-as-a-batch","content":"For example:"},"325":{"id":"/reviews-21","page_id":"/reviews","type":"text","url":"/reviews#5-send-comments-as-a-batch","content":"or with extra guidance:"},"326":{"id":"/reviews-22","page_id":"/reviews","type":"text","url":"/reviews#5-send-comments-as-a-batch","content":"Pochi will process every line comment with context and update the code accordingly."},"327":{"id":"/rules","page_id":"/rules","type":"page","content":"Rules","url":"/rules"},"328":{"id":"/rules-0","page_id":"/rules","type":"text","url":"/rules","content":"Define coding standards and development guidelines"},"329":{"id":"/rules-1","page_id":"/rules","type":"heading","url":"/rules#rules","content":"Rules"},"330":{"id":"/rules-2","page_id":"/rules","type":"heading","url":"/rules#example","content":"Example"},"331":{"id":"/rules-3","page_id":"/rules","type":"heading","url":"/rules#locations","content":"Locations"},"332":{"id":"/rules-4","page_id":"/rules","type":"heading","url":"/rules#workspace","content":"Workspace"},"333":{"id":"/rules-5","page_id":"/rules","type":"heading","url":"/rules#global","content":"Global"},"334":{"id":"/rules-6","page_id":"/rules","type":"text","url":"/rules#rules","content":"You can provide custom instructions to Pochi by creating an README.pochi.md file. This is similar to CLAUDE.md or Cursor’s rules."},"335":{"id":"/rules-7","page_id":"/rules","type":"text","url":"/rules#rules","content":"title: AGENTS.md support"},"336":{"id":"/rules-8","page_id":"/rules","type":"text","url":"/rules#rules","content":"Pochi also supports AGENTS.md as an alternative to README.pochi.md. Both files serve the same purpose and are treated identically by Pochi."},"337":{"id":"/rules-9","page_id":"/rules","type":"text","url":"/rules#example","content":"Below example is the README.pochi.md file for Pochi itself."},"338":{"id":"/rules-10","page_id":"/rules","type":"text","url":"/rules#locations","content":"Pochi looks for rules in two locations:"},"339":{"id":"/rules-11","page_id":"/rules","type":"text","url":"/rules#workspace","content":"Pochi first checks for a README.pochi.md (or AGENTS.md) file in your current workspace root directory. This is where you define project-specific rules that apply only to your current project."},"340":{"id":"/rules-12","page_id":"/rules","type":"text","url":"/rules#global","content":"Pochi also reads global rules defined in ~/.pochi/README.pochi.md. These rules apply to all projects and are suitable for any personal rules that Pochi should follow."},"341":{"id":"/rules-13","page_id":"/rules","type":"text","url":"/rules#global","content":"You can view current active rules in toolbar's token usage popover"},"342":{"id":"/share","page_id":"/share","type":"page","content":"Share","url":"/share"},"343":{"id":"/share-0","page_id":"/share","type":"text","url":"/share","content":"Share your development context with team members"},"344":{"id":"/share-1","page_id":"/share","type":"heading","url":"/share#share","content":"Share"},"345":{"id":"/share-2","page_id":"/share","type":"heading","url":"/share#how-it-works","content":"How it works"},"346":{"id":"/share-3","page_id":"/share","type":"text","url":"/share#share","content":"The Share feature in Pochi's toolbar allows you to share your current development context with others."},"347":{"id":"/share-4","page_id":"/share","type":"text","url":"/share#share","content":"type: info"},"348":{"id":"/share-5","page_id":"/share","type":"text","url":"/share#share","content":"title: Public Access"},"349":{"id":"/share-6","page_id":"/share","type":"text","url":"/share#share","content":"Shared conversations are publicly accessible to anyone with the link. Do not share sensitive information or private code."},"350":{"id":"/share-7","page_id":"/share","type":"text","url":"/share#how-it-works","content":"When you share a conversation, Pochi:"},"351":{"id":"/share-8","page_id":"/share","type":"text","url":"/share#how-it-works","content":"Persist your task to our servers, and create a unique public URL for the task.."},"352":{"id":"/share-9","page_id":"/share","type":"text","url":"/share#how-it-works","content":"Makes task accessible via a link - app.getpochi.com/share/<shareId>"},"353":{"id":"/skills","page_id":"/skills","type":"page","content":"Skills","url":"/skills"},"354":{"id":"/skills-0","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills","content":"Define reusable behavior via SKILL.md definitions"},"355":{"id":"/skills-1","page_id":"/skills","type":"heading","url":"/skills#install-skills","content":"Install Skills"},"356":{"id":"/skills-2","page_id":"/skills","type":"heading","url":"/skills#create-skills","content":"Create Skills"},"357":{"id":"/skills-3","page_id":"/skills","type":"heading","url":"/skills#example","content":"Example"},"358":{"id":"/skills-4","page_id":"/skills","type":"heading","url":"/skills#frontmatter","content":"Frontmatter"},"359":{"id":"/skills-5","page_id":"/skills","type":"heading","url":"/skills#discovery","content":"Discovery"},"360":{"id":"/skills-6","page_id":"/skills","type":"heading","url":"/skills#cross-agent-compatibility","content":"Cross-Agent Compatibility"},"361":{"id":"/skills-7","page_id":"/skills","type":"heading","url":"/skills#using-skills","content":"Using Skills"},"362":{"id":"/skills-8","page_id":"/skills","type":"heading","url":"/skills#viewing-available-skills","content":"Viewing Available Skills"},"363":{"id":"/skills-9","page_id":"/skills","type":"heading","url":"/skills#activating-skills","content":"Activating Skills"},"364":{"id":"/skills-10","page_id":"/skills","type":"heading","url":"/skills#automatic-discovery","content":"Automatic Discovery"},"365":{"id":"/skills-11","page_id":"/skills","type":"heading","url":"/skills#slash-commands","content":"Slash Commands"},"366":{"id":"/skills-12","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills","content":"Skills are reusable instruction sets that extend Pochi's capabilities. They allow you to standardize workflows, provide domain-specific knowledge, or integrate with external tools."},"367":{"id":"/skills-13","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#install-skills","content":"You can discover and install skills from the community skills.sh registry using the CLI:"},"368":{"id":"/skills-14","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#install-skills","content":"This command automatically detects Pochi and installs the skill to .pochi/skills in your project. Alternatively, you can place skills in .agents/skills/ to share them with other AI coding agents."},"369":{"id":"/skills-15","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#create-skills","content":"To create a custom skill, place a SKILL.md file in a subdirectory of .pochi/skills/."},"370":{"id":"/skills-16","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#create-skills","content":"File path: .pochi/skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md"},"371":{"id":"/skills-17","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#example","content":"Here is an example SKILL.md for creating GitHub issues:"},"372":{"id":"/skills-18","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#frontmatter","content":"Each skill must start with YAML frontmatter containing at least a name and description."},"373":{"id":"/skills-19","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#frontmatter","content":"Field"},"374":{"id":"/skills-20","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#frontmatter","content":"Description"},"375":{"id":"/skills-21","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#frontmatter","content":"name"},"376":{"id":"/skills-22","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#frontmatter","content":"Unique identifier (lowercase, hyphens allowed)."},"377":{"id":"/skills-23","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#frontmatter","content":"description"},"378":{"id":"/skills-24","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#frontmatter","content":"Brief explanation of what the skill does."},"379":{"id":"/skills-25","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#frontmatter","content":"disable-model-invocation"},"380":{"id":"/skills-26","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#frontmatter","content":"Set to true to exclude the Skill from model discovery and reject useSkill invocation. Defaults to false."},"381":{"id":"/skills-27","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#frontmatter","content":"user-invocable"},"382":{"id":"/skills-28","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#frontmatter","content":"Set to false to hide and reject the /name command. Defaults to true."},"383":{"id":"/skills-29","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#frontmatter","content":"The two invocation controls are independent. Set disable-model-invocation: true for a manual-only Skill, user-invocable: false for a model-only Skill, or both to disable all invocation paths. Manual invocation expands the Skill instructions directly without exposing it through the useSkill tool."},"384":{"id":"/skills-30","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#discovery","content":"Pochi automatically discovers skills in the following locations (higher priority listed first):"},"385":{"id":"/skills-31","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#discovery","content":"Project: .pochi/skills/ (shared with your team, Pochi-specific)"},"386":{"id":"/skills-32","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#discovery","content":"Project: .agents/skills/ (shared with your team, cross-agent standard)"},"387":{"id":"/skills-33","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#discovery","content":"Global: ~/.pochi/skills/ (available across all projects, Pochi-specific)"},"388":{"id":"/skills-34","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#discovery","content":"Global: ~/.agents/skills/ (available across all projects, cross-agent standard)"},"389":{"id":"/skills-35","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#discovery","content":"If two skills share the same name, the one from the higher-priority location takes precedence."},"390":{"id":"/skills-36","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#cross-agent-compatibility","content":"The .agents/ directory is an emerging standard shared by multiple AI coding agents (e.g., Claude Code, Codex). By placing skills in .agents/skills/, you can define shared workflows once and have them available across different agents without duplicating files."},"391":{"id":"/skills-37","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#viewing-available-skills","content":"You can view all available skills in your settings panel. This gives you an overview of all installed skills. You can also click the edit button on the right side of each skill to open and modify the corresponding skill file."},"392":{"id":"/skills-38","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#activating-skills","content":"There are two ways to activate skills in Pochi:"},"393":{"id":"/skills-39","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#automatic-discovery","content":"Pochi can automatically discover and invoke relevant skills based on your prompt. When you describe what you want to do, Pochi will analyze your request and suggest appropriate skills to use."},"394":{"id":"/skills-40","page_id":"/skills","type":"text","url":"/skills#slash-commands","content":"You can explicitly specify which skill to use by typing a slash command followed by the skill name. This gives you direct control over which skill gets activated."},"395":{"id":"/tab-completion","page_id":"/tab-completion","type":"page","content":"Tab Completion","url":"/tab-completion"},"396":{"id":"/tab-completion-0","page_id":"/tab-completion","type":"text","url":"/tab-completion","content":"Inline code completion"},"397":{"id":"/tab-completion-1","page_id":"/tab-completion","type":"heading","url":"/tab-completion#tab-completion","content":"Tab Completion"},"398":{"id":"/tab-completion-2","page_id":"/tab-completion","type":"heading","url":"/tab-completion#multi-language-support","content":"Multi-Language Support"},"399":{"id":"/tab-completion-3","page_id":"/tab-completion","type":"heading","url":"/tab-completion#using-tab-completion","content":"Using Tab Completion"},"400":{"id":"/tab-completion-4","page_id":"/tab-completion","type":"heading","url":"/tab-completion#keyboard-shortcuts","content":"Keyboard Shortcuts"},"401":{"id":"/tab-completion-5","page_id":"/tab-completion","type":"heading","url":"/tab-completion#status-bar-item","content":