age_id":"/vscode","type":"heading","url":"/vscode#installation","content":"Installation"},"457":{"id":"/vscode-2","page_id":"/vscode","type":"heading","url":"/vscode#welcome","content":"Welcome"},"458":{"id":"/vscode-3","page_id":"/vscode","type":"heading","url":"/vscode#chat","content":"Chat"},"459":{"id":"/vscode-4","page_id":"/vscode","type":"heading","url":"/vscode#prompting","content":"Prompting"},"460":{"id":"/vscode-5","page_id":"/vscode","type":"heading","url":"/vscode#tasks","content":"Tasks"},"461":{"id":"/vscode-6","page_id":"/vscode","type":"heading","url":"/vscode#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"462":{"id":"/vscode-7","page_id":"/vscode","type":"text","url":"/vscode#vs-code","content":"This page covers the core Pochi experience in VS Code, from installation and setup to the main chat and task management features."},"463":{"id":"/vscode-8","page_id":"/vscode","type":"text","url":"/vscode#installation","content":"Install the Pochi extension from the VS Code Marketplace or OpenVSX."},"464":{"id":"/vscode-9","page_id":"/vscode","type":"text","url":"/vscode#installation","content":"For the best experience, we recommend dragging the Pochi view to the right sidebar to use it side-by-side with your editor."},"465":{"id":"/vscode-10","page_id":"/vscode","type":"text","url":"/vscode#welcome","content":"Upon first launch, Pochi's Welcome page offers two ways to get started:"},"466":{"id":"/vscode-11","page_id":"/vscode","type":"text","url":"/vscode#welcome","content":"Sign in to Pochi: Click \"Sign In\" and authorize in your browser to use Pochi subscriptions, models, and cloud features."},"467":{"id":"/vscode-12","page_id":"/vscode","type":"text","url":"/vscode#welcome","content":"Bring Your Own Key (BYOK): Use your own models by running Pochi: Open Custom Model Settings from the Command Palette. This opens ~/.pochi/config.jsonc for you to add API keys. See Models for details."},"468":{"id":"/vscode-13","page_id":"/vscode","type":"text","url":"/vscode#chat","content":"Access the Pochi chat panel via the Activity Bar icon or shortcut (macOS: Cmd+L, Win/Linux: Ctrl+L). This is your main interface for interacting with Pochi. Note: An active workspace (i.e., an open folder) is required to use the chat."},"469":{"id":"/vscode-14","page_id":"/vscode","type":"text","url":"/vscode#chat","content":"The panel's title bar includes actions for starting a new task and viewing all tasks."},"470":{"id":"/vscode-15","page_id":"/vscode","type":"text","url":"/vscode#prompting","content":"The input box, located below the chat history, is where you'll compose your messages and control the chat."},"471":{"id":"/vscode-16","page_id":"/vscode","type":"text","url":"/vscode#prompting","content":"Auto-Approve Menu: This menu at the top of the zone allows you to grant Pochi permission to use tools autonomously, streamlining the workflow."},"472":{"id":"/vscode-17","page_id":"/vscode","type":"text","url":"/vscode#prompting","content":"Todo List: When Pochi creates a to-do list for a task, it will appear here, allowing you to track progress."},"473":{"id":"/vscode-18","page_id":"/vscode","type":"text","url":"/vscode#prompting","content":"Chat Input: The main text area supports both text and image uploads. You can attach files by clicking the paperclip icon or by dragging and dropping them into the input area."},"474":{"id":"/vscode-19","page_id":"/vscode","type":"text","url":"/vscode#prompting","content":"Bottom Toolbar: The toolbar at the very bottom provides several key functions:"},"475":{"id":"/vscode-20","page_id":"/vscode","type":"text","url":"/vscode#prompting","content":"Model Selector: Choose which language model you want to interact with."},"476":{"id":"/vscode-21","page_id":"/vscode","type":"text","url":"/vscode#prompting","content":"Token Usage & Compact Task: Monitor the token count of your conversation. If the conversation becomes long, a Compact Task button will appear, allowing you to condense the history and save tokens."},"477":{"id":"/vscode-22","page_id":"/vscode","type":"text","url":"/vscode#prompting","content":"Sharing: Share your chat session with others (requires a Pochi account)."},"478":{"id":"/vscode-23","page_id":"/vscode","type":"text","url":"/vscode#prompting","content":"Submit/Stop Button: The send button dynamically transforms into a stop button during message generation, allowing you to interrupt the AI at any time."},"479":{"id":"/vscode-24","page_id":"/vscode","type":"text","url":"/vscode#tasks","content":"A chat session in Pochi is saved as a Task. You can view your entire task history from the task list page."},"480":{"id":"/vscode-25","page_id":"/vscode","type":"text","url":"/vscode#tasks","content":"Some AI-powered actions might generate a Sub-task, which is a new, focused chat session dedicated to a specific part of the original task.\nWhen you're in a sub-task, you'll see a \"Back\" button to navigate to the parent task, allowing you to maintain context while breaking down complex problems.\nBy default sub-tasks are hidden in the task list."},"481":{"id":"/vscode-26","page_id":"/vscode","type":"text","url":"/vscode#tasks","content":"By default, task history is stored locally. Signing in to a Pochi account enables cloud storage for your tasks, along with sharing and team collaboration features.\nBe aware that clearing VS Code's extension data may erase your local task history."},"482":{"id":"/vscode-27","page_id":"/vscode","type":"text","url":"/vscode#troubleshooting","content":"Having issues? Here are a few things to check:"},"483":{"id":"/vscode-28","page_id":"/vscode","type":"text","url":"/vscode#troubleshooting","content":"No Active Workspace: Pochi requires an open folder to function correctly. Make sure you have a workspace open."},"484":{"id":"/vscode-29","page_id":"/vscode","type":"text","url":"/vscode#troubleshooting","content":"Sign-in/Model Configuration: Verify that you are either signed in to your Pochi account or have a valid API key configured in your ~/.pochi/config.jsonc."},"485":{"id":"/vscode-30","page_id":"/vscode","type":"text","url":"/vscode#troubleshooting","content":"For more help, check the full Troubleshooting page or join our community on Discord."},"486":{"id":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1","page_id":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1","type":"page","content":"Weekly Update","url":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1"},"487":{"id":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1-0","page_id":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1","type":"heading","url":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1#weekly-update-1","content":"Weekly Update #1"},"488":{"id":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1-1","page_id":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1","type":"heading","url":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1#tldr","content":"TL;DR"},"489":{"id":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1-2","page_id":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1","type":"heading","url":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1#enhancements-","content":"Enhancements ✨"},"490":{"id":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1-3","page_id":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1","type":"heading","url":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1#bug-fixes-","content":"Bug Fixes 🐛"},"491":{"id":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1-4","page_id":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1","type":"text","url":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1#tldr","content":"This week we polished the VS Code extension with some UX upgrades, open-sourced the Pochi CLI, and did a few rounds of codebase cleanup to make contributing easier and friendlier for newcomers. We look forward to your first visit to the repo!"},"492":{"id":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1-5","page_id":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1","type":"text","url":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1#enhancements-","content":"Drag & drop images: Share visuals with Pochi in the VS Code chat just by dragging them in. #64"},"493":{"id":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1-6","page_id":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1","type":"text","url":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1#enhancements-","content":"Improved docs: Updated structure and added guidance on model settings for easier use. #60, #63 , 900d162"},"494":{"id":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1-7","page_id":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1","type":"text","url":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1#enhancements-","content":"Model pricing at your fingertips: Check model costs directly in settings before choosing one. #74"},"495":{"id":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1-8","page_id":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1","type":"text","url":"/developer-updates/2025-08-29-weekly-update-1#bug-fixes-","content":"File search now correctly surfaces matching files: Queries that used to return empty results will now behave as expected. #79"},"496":{"id":"/developer-updates/2025-09-05-weekly-update-2","page_id":"/developer-updates/2025-09-05-weekly-update-2","type":"page","content":"Weekly Update","url":"/developer-updates/2025-09-05-weekly-update-2"},"497":{"id":"/developer-updates/2025-09-05-weekly-update-2-0","page_id":"/developer-updates/2025-09-05-weekly-update-2","type":"heading","url":"/developer-updates/2025-09-05-weekly-update-2#weekly-update-2","content":"Weekly Update #2"},"498":{"id":"/developer-updates/2025-09-05-weekly-update-2-1","page_id":"/developer-updates/2025-09-05-weekly-update-2","type":"heading","url":"/developer-updates/2025-09-05-weekly-update-2#tldr","content":"TL;DR"},"499":{"id":"/developer-updates/2025-09-05-weekly-update-2-2","page_id":"/developer-updates/2025-09-05-weekly-update-2","type":"heading","url":"/developer-updates/2025-09-05-weekly-update-2#features-","content":"Features 🚀"},"500":{"id":"/developer-updates/