t Coordination"},"3235":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-28","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#when-to-use-parallel-agents-and-when-not-to","content":"When to Use Parallel Agents (and When Not To)"},"3236":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-29","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#common-issues","content":"Common Issues"},"3237":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-30","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#conclusion","content":"Conclusion"},"3238":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-31","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#key-takeaways","content":"Key Takeaways"},"3239":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-32","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#why-use-parallel-agents","content":"When working with AI agents, you'll hit a bottleneck: sequential execution is slow."},"3240":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-33","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#why-use-parallel-agents","content":"A single AI agent completes task A → waits → then task B → waits → then task C. Three 15-minute tasks executed sequentially would take 45 minutes in total. In software development, for example, one agent builds the backend API → then the frontend → then writes tests."},"3241":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-34","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#why-use-parallel-agents","content":"In practice, teams often work in parallel. Different specialists work in parallel, coordinating through shared specifications."},"3242":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-35","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#why-use-parallel-agents","content":"That's what Pochi's Parallel Agents solve. Run multiple agents concurrently—each in its own isolated workspace, all working with shared context and background. Complete multiple tasks simultaneously."},"3243":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-36","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#what-you-will-learn","content":"Creating Git worktrees for isolated development"},"3244":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-37","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#what-you-will-learn","content":"Running parallel agents on concurrent tasks"},"3245":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-38","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#what-you-will-learn","content":"Best practices for developing a new project from scratch"},"3246":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-39","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#what-you-will-learn","content":"We'll build a weather demo application to show these concepts in practice."},"3247":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-40","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#prerequisites","content":"Install Pochi and ensure it is running in Visual Studio Code."},"3248":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-41","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#prerequisites","content":"Node.js (version 18+) and npm installed"},"3249":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-42","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#prerequisites","content":"Git installed and configured on your system"},"3250":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-43","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#how-it-works","content":"Pochi's Parallel Agents run multiple AI agents concurrently, each in its own Git worktree with an isolated branch. Agents work independently on different tasks while sharing the same repository context, allowing you to complete multiple components simultaneously without conflicts."},"3251":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-44","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#how-it-works","content":"Learn more in the Parallel Agents documentation."},"3252":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-45","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#getting-started-building-a-weather-demo-with-parallel-agents","content":"In this hands-on tutorial, we'll build a complete weather application using Pochi's Parallel Agents feature. You'll see how to coordinate multiple agents working in parallel on frontend, backend, and testing tasks - demonstrating the power of concurrent development."},"3253":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-46","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#getting-started-building-a-weather-demo-with-parallel-agents","content":"The development workflow for this project looks like this:"},"3254":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-47","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#step-1-set-up-the-environment-and-initialize-the-project","content":"First, we'll create a new Next.js project using create-next-app, which will automatically set up the project structure and initialize a Git repository for our parallel development workflow."},"3255":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-48","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#step-2-write-a-design-document","content":"A well-structured design document is crucial when working with parallel agents. It serves as the single source of truth that all agents will reference to understand the project requirements, architecture, and their specific responsibilities."},"3256":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-49","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#create-the-design-document","content":"Create a file docs/design.md with the following content:"},"3257":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-50","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#commit-the-design-document","content":"This design document provides clear specifications that each parallel agent can reference when working on their respective tasks. It defines a weather application that fetches real data from Open-Meteo API (including geocoding and weather forecasts), specifying data structures, API contracts, and UI requirements for independent parallel implementation."},"3258":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-51","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#step-3-create-git-worktrees-for-parallel-tasks","content":"Now we'll create three separate worktrees, each with its own branch, for the three parallel development tasks: frontend, backend, and test."},"3259":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-52","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#method-1-using-pochi-sidebar","content":"You can create worktrees from the Pochi sidebar using \"New worktree\" mode. Simply start chatting with a prompt, and Pochi will automatically create a new worktree and launch the agent task:"},"3260":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-53","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-age