izing the browser window"},"3290":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-83","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#verify-integration","content":"If everything works as expected, you've successfully built a complete application using parallel agents."},"3291":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-84","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#verify-integration","content":"Here's what mine looks like - pretty cool, right? And the best part: the code generated by the agents worked on the first try and passed all tests! The entire process took about 5 minutes—without parallel agents, a single agent would have needed around 15 minutes to complete all three tasks sequentially."},"3292":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-85","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#agent-coordination","content":"Consistent Design Document: Ensure your design document is detailed and clear. All agents reference this document, so ambiguity can lead to inconsistent implementations."},"3293":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-86","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#agent-coordination","content":"API Contracts: Clearly define API contracts (endpoints, request/response formats) in the design document so frontend and backend agents align perfectly."},"3294":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-87","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#agent-coordination","content":"Version Control: Commit the design document before creating worktrees so all agents have access to the latest specifications."},"3295":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-88","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#when-to-use-parallel-agents-and-when-not-to","content":"Good fit for parallel agents:"},"3296":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-89","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#when-to-use-parallel-agents-and-when-not-to","content":"Different roles, parallel completion - Frontend, backend, tests working simultaneously"},"3297":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-90","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#when-to-use-parallel-agents-and-when-not-to","content":"Independent tasks - Querying multiple websites and aggregating results"},"3298":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-91","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#when-to-use-parallel-agents-and-when-not-to","content":"Batch processing - Generating test reports, review reports for multiple modules"},"3299":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-92","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#when-to-use-parallel-agents-and-when-not-to","content":"Not a good fit:"},"3300":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-93","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#when-to-use-parallel-agents-and-when-not-to","content":"Strong dependencies - Requirements doc → design doc → implementation must be sequential"},"3301":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-94","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#when-to-use-parallel-agents-and-when-not-to","content":"Complex reasoning with continuous context - Mathematical proofs, chain-of-thought problems"},"3302":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-95","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#when-to-use-parallel-agents-and-when-not-to","content":"High conflict resolution cost - Multiple agents heavily modifying the same files"},"3303":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-96","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#common-issues","content":"Issue: Agent can't access design document"},"3304":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-97","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#common-issues","content":"Solution: Ensure the design document is committed to the main branch before creating worktrees."},"3305":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-98","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#common-issues","content":"Issue: API integration fails between frontend and backend"},"3306":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-99","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#common-issues","content":"Solution: Verify API endpoint URLs and response formats match the design document specifications."},"3307":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-100","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#common-issues","content":"Issue: Worktree conflicts during merge"},"3308":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-101","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#common-issues","content":"Solution: Review the design document for any ambiguous specifications. Update and have agents revise their implementations if needed."},"3309":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-102","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#conclusion","content":"Congratulations! You've successfully used Pochi's Parallel Agents to build a complete weather application with frontend, backend, and tests developed concurrently. This tutorial demonstrated how parallel agents can dramatically accelerate development by allowing multiple components to be built simultaneously."},"3310":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-103","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#key-takeaways","content":"Git Worktrees: Leveraging Git worktrees provides isolation while maintaining connection to the same repository."},"3311":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-104","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#key-takeaways","content":"Parallel Agent Development: Multiple agents working in isolated worktrees enable true parallel development without conflicts."},"3312":{"id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance-105","page_id":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/parallel-agent-guidance#key-takeaways","content":"Design Documents: A clear, comprehensive design document is essential for coordinating multiple agents."},"3313":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"page","content":"Secure Production DB Access in Pochi","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi"},"3314":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-0","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","content":"This tutorial demonstrates how to grant database access in Pochi without exposing production credentials or enabling uncontrolled writes."},"3315":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-1","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#secure-production-db-access-in-pochi","content":"Secure Production DB Access in Pochi"},"3316":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-2","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#why-this-matters","content":"Why this matters"},"3317":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-3","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites"},"3318":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-4","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#tier-1-read-only-inspection","content":"Tier 1: Read-only inspection"},"3319":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-5","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-1-create-a-read-only-postgres-role","content":"Step 1: Create a read-only Postgres role"},"3320":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-6","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-2-mcp-server-read-only-tools","content":"Step 2: MCP Server (read-only tools)"},"3321":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-7","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-3-configure-pochi","content":"Step 3: Configure Pochi"},"3322":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-8","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-4-disable-execution-surface","content":"Step 4: Disable execution surface"},"3323":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-9","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#tier-2--safe-writes-via-clone--pipeline-demo","content":"Tier 2:  Safe writes via clone + pipeline (demo)"},"3324":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-10","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-1-architecture","content":"Step 1: Architecture"},"3325":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-11","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-2-add-a-production-inspection-tool","content":"Step 2: Add a production inspection tool"},"3326":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-12","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-3-create-a-writable-clone","content":"Step 3: Create a writable clone"},"3327":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-13","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-4-setup-validation-mcp","content":"Step 4: Setup Validation MCP"},"3328":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-14","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-5-plan-pochi-plan-mode","content":"Step 5: Plan (Pochi Plan Mode)"},"3329":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-15","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-6-generate-migration-script","content":"Step 6: Generate Migration Script"},"3330":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-16","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-7-validate-in-clone","content":"Step 7: Validate in Clone"},"3331":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-17","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-8-deploy-to-production-manual--approved-pipeline","content":"Step 8: Deploy to Production (Manual + Approved Pipeline)"},"3332":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-18","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#how-this-maps-to-real-production-setups","content":"How this maps to real production setups"},"3333":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-19","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#conclusion","content":"Conclusion"},"3334":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-20","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#secure-production-db-access-in-pochi","content":"We previously examined common approaches teams use to protect production databases (i.e. command allowlists, SQL filters, and manual approval workflows) and why they fail in the presence of autonomous agents."},"3335":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-21","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#secure-production-db-access-in-pochi","content":"The primary reason is that agents \"work really hard\" - they often route around these restrictions to deliver the results with any possible execution surface (shell, file system, runtime)."},"3336":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-22","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#secure-production-db-access-in-pochi","content":"This tutorial demonstrates how to grant database access in Pochi without exposing production credentials or enabling uncontrolled writes."},"3337":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-23","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#why-this-matters","content":"Agents must never execute arbitrary code against production systems. At the same time, agents are most useful when they can read and write data to iterate quickly. The challenge is doing this safely."},"3338":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-24","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#why-this-matters","content":"We’ll walk through multiple access tiers, explain their security tradeoffs, and show how to progressively increase agent autonomy without expanding the production attack surface."},"3339":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-25","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#prerequisites","content":"Before we start, you’ll need the following:"},"3340":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-26","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#prerequisites","content":"Node.js installed"},"3341":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-27","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#prerequisites","content":"PostgreSQL running"},"3342":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-28","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#prerequisites","content":"title: Note"},"3343":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-29","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#prerequisites","content":"Before following along, do note that this tutorial is a demo. Don’t expose credentials in real systems and always use secrets managers."},"3344":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-30","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#tier-1-read-only-inspection","content":"To make sure that an agent never connects to the database directly, a common first step is to provide read-only access via a tool interface. The tool service owns the database credentials and strictly constrains the queries that can be executed."},"3345":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-31","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#tier-1-read-only-inspection","content":"For our demo, we’ll use an MCP HTTP service that exposes a fixed set of read-only tools. Production data will be accessible only through this interface."},"3346":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-32","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-1-create-a-read-only-postgres-role","content":"We’ll use a Postgres database. To create one, run the following command in your terminal:"},"3347":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-33","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-1-create-a-read-only-postgres-role","content":"Next, we create a dedicated database role whose permissions enforce read-only access at the database layer:"},"3348":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-34","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-1-create-a-read-only-postgres-role","content":"Continue over to add a new table:"},"3349":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-35","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-1-create-a-read-only-postgres-role","content":"Now we proceed to add data. Here's a sample to get you started:"},"3350":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-36","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-2-mcp-server-read-only-tools","content":"Next, we implement a minimal MCP server (server.js) :"},"3351":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-37","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-2-mcp-server-read-only-tools","content":"In this MCP server, we expose a narrowly scoped tool called recent_orders that allows us to filter the most recent orders in a given time period."},"3352":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-38","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-3-configure-pochi","content":"Now we configure Pochi to use the MCP. For that, let's add to config.jsonc:"},"3353":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-39","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-3-configure-pochi","content":"From the agent’s perspective, the only available interface to production data is the MCP tool API. To test this theory, let’s give the agent a read-only prompt:"},"3354":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-40","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-3-configure-pochi","content":"Your browser does not support the video tag."},"3355":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-41","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-3-configure-pochi","content":"As expected, the agent invokes the recent_orders tool and gets the corresponding output. Since there was no write operation involved, there was no direct database access."},"3356":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-42","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-3-configure-pochi","content":"So far, this looks safe."},"3357":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-43","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-3-configure-pochi","content":"Next, let’s ask the agent to modify some data."},"3358":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-44","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-3-configure-pochi","content":"Since there is no MCP tool capable of performing writes, the expected behaviour is for execution to fail."},"3359":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-45","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-3-configure-pochi","content":"Instead of failing, the agent searches for alternative execution paths to complete the task when its first few attempts to do a write operation fails. It searches the code for database-related code, generates a small Node.js script using the pg client and executes it through the shell. This ends up updating the database directly."},"3360":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-46","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-3-configure-pochi","content":"Your browser does not support the video tag."},"3361":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-47","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-3-configure-pochi","content":"If you look closely, the agent simply completed the task using an execution path that still existed because we left that gap open."},"3362":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-48","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-3-configure-pochi","content":"From this, we conclude that since the agent can be given shell access, database credentials, or the ability to construct queries, the security boundary still lives inside the model rather than the system."},"3363":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-49","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-4-disable-execution-surface","content":"To actually make the setup read-only, two additional controls can be applied. First, we explicitly revoke database writes:"},"3364":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-50","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-4-disable-execution-surface","content":"Second, we disable execution permissions in the editor."},"3365":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-51","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-4-disable-execution-surface","content":"This approach removes the entire class of risk. From Pochi’s standpoint, this means the agent cannot run any shell commands, write files, or execute programs. The only remaining interface was the MCP tool API, which is equivalent to calling a standard, credential-isolated API to query production data."},"3366":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-52","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-4-disable-execution-surface","content":"Following this, the read requests continued to work as expected from before. The agent used the MCP tools and returned the proper output. But now, when asked again to do a write operation:"},"3367":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-53","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-4-disable-execution-surface","content":"The agent could still reason about how to perform updates, and could still propose code in the editor, but it no longer had the ability to apply or execute those changes without explicit human approval. The task remained incomplete by design."},"3368":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-54","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-4-disable-execution-surface","content":"Your browser does not support the video tag."},"3369":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-55","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-4-disable-execution-surface","content":"That being said, production was still accessible through the same execution surface, requiring constant human oversight. This could lead to problems where a human might blindly click ‘Save’ or settings may have auto-approve write enabled by default."},"3370":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-56","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-4-disable-execution-surface","content":"While this may appear operational, it is strongly recommended to avoid granting even read access to production databases due to the unpredictable nature of agents. Agents are non-deterministic by design, and production systems should not be exposed to that uncertainty."},"3371":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-57","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-4-disable-execution-surface","content":"But the challenge remains that many legitimate tasks still require writes. This leads us to the next tier of access."},"3372":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-58","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#tier-2--safe-writes-via-clone--pipeline-demo","content":"Granting an agent direct write access to production is dangerous. Even if you try to enforce human approvals, the agent can still find ways to bypass restrictions if it has any execution surface."},"3373":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-59","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#tier-2--safe-writes-via-clone--pipeline-demo","content":"The safer approach is to strictly separate reasoning from execution."},"3374":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-60","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#tier-2--safe-writes-via-clone--pipeline-demo","content":"For this we'll use an Isolated Work Environment (IWE). The agent can generate and test migration scripts in a writable clone of the database (IWE), but the production database remains locked down. Once the migration is validated on the clone, the same script is applied to production through the normal deployment pipeline, with human approval and rollback controls."},"3375":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-61","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#tier-2--safe-writes-via-clone--pipeline-demo","content":"Let’s have a look at what this looks like in a complete flow."},"3376":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-62","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#tier-2--safe-writes-via-clone--pipeline-demo","content":"Continuing our example from before, we found that many paid orders in production were missing the total amount value. The correct total for an order should be:"},"3377":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-63","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#tier-2--safe-writes-via-clone--pipeline-demo","content":"We want to backfill all orders where the total IS NULL. At the same time, we also do not want to give the agent write access to production."},"3378":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-64","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-1-architecture","content":"In order to enforce isolation, we’ll run two separate MCP services."},"3379":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-65","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-1-architecture","content":"Production MCP: This will be connected to our existing database, i.e. shop_sandbox, which has a read-only DB role"},"3380":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-66","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-1-architecture","content":"Validation MCP: This will be connected to a clone of shop_sandbox named shop_validate and will have a write-capable DB role."},"3381":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-67","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-1-architecture","content":"Each MCP server will have its own database credentials and expose its own tool interface. From the agent’s point of view, the only way to interact with a database is by calling tools exposed by whichever MCP servers are enabled for the task."},"3382":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-68","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-2-add-a-production-inspection-tool","content":"As seen earlier,  shop_sandbox is locked down. The agent can only query it via MCP read-only tools. The database role for this MCP has only SELECT permission, and shell access is disabled in agent tasks."},"3383":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-69","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-2-add-a-production-inspection-tool","content":"Previously, we only exposed the recent_orders tool via this MCP. Now we’ll introduce the orders_missing_totals tool:"},"3384":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-70","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-2-add-a-production-inspection-tool","content":"To check if everything works as expected, let’s run a sample prompt:"},"3385":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-71","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-2-add-a-production-inspection-tool","content":"Your browser does not support the video tag."},"3386":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-72","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-2-add-a-production-inspection-tool","content":"As seen, the agent can inspect how many orders are missing a total field, but it cannot modify anything on the production database."},"3387":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-73","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-3-create-a-writable-clone","content":"Next, we create a writeable clone of  shop_sandbox  named  shop_validate with the same schema and data."},"3388":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-74","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-3-create-a-writable-clone","content":"Create a write-capable role for validation:"},"3389":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-75","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-3-create-a-writable-clone","content":"Grant database and schema access:"},"3390":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-76","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-4-setup-validation-mcp","content":"Add the new server to config.jsonc:"},"3391":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-77","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-4-setup-validation-mcp","content":"This new MCP will be our environment for the agent to perform writes. It will expose two tools: execute_sql and run_migration_file."},"3392":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-78","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-4-setup-validation-mcp","content":"This way, we give Validation MCP the ability perform write operations while Production MCP only has read access. For the purpose of this blog, this is how we achieved environment isolation by routing the agent to different tool backends."},"3393":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-79","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-5-plan-pochi-plan-mode","content":"Next, we will use Pochi’s plan mode to create a migration plan. Since Pochi allows us to enable MCP per task, we can use Validation MCP to perform the write operations."},"3394":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-80","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-5-plan-pochi-plan-mode","content":"Your browser does not support the video tag."},"3395":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-81","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-5-plan-pochi-plan-mode","content":"To start with Plan mode we insert the below prompt and click on Plan in the prompt-send option:"},"3396":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-82","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-5-plan-pochi-plan-mode","content":"Your browser does not support the video tag."},"3397":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-83","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-5-plan-pochi-plan-mode","content":"So far there is no database access involved. You can review the plan, put inline comments and Pochi will modify the plan based on your inputs."},"3398":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-84","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-5-plan-pochi-plan-mode","content":"Your browser does not support the video tag."},"3399":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-85","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-6-generate-migration-script","content":"Once you have the plan finalised, you can generate a migration script. To do so, we prompt back to Pochi:"},"3400":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-86","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-6-generate-migration-script","content":"Your browser does not support the video tag."},"3401":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-87","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-6-generate-migration-script","content":"Pochi generates the following migration file, which can now be reviewed, versioned, and audited:"},"3402":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-88","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-6-generate-migration-script","content":"At this point, still no database values have been modified."},"3403":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-89","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-7-validate-in-clone","content":"Now, with only validation MCP enabled, we can ask Pochi to do a write operation by applying the migration to the shop_validate database."},"3404":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-90","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-7-validate-in-clone","content":"Your browser does not support the video tag."},"3405":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-91","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-7-validate-in-clone","content":"Pochi will read the SQL file, send the SQL to validation MCP service, which will update shop_validate database."},"3406":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-92","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-7-validate-in-clone","content":"Before:"},"3407":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-93","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-7-validate-in-clone","content":"After:"},"3408":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-94","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-7-validate-in-clone","content":"All this time production database shop_sandbox remains untouched."},"3409":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-95","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-7-validate-in-clone","content":"Now if the changes are incorrect or you would like modifications, you can prompt back Pochi. For eg:"},"3410":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-96","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-7-validate-in-clone","content":"The agent will try new SQL and rerun in validation."},"3411":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-97","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-7-validate-in-clone","content":"Once you are happy with the changes you can update the SQL file:"},"3412":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-98","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-8-deploy-to-production-manual--approved-pipeline","content":"Once validation looks good, production updates can be performed manually or via an approved deployment pipeline. In our case, we run the following command to apply the changes from shop_validate to shop_database."},"3413":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-99","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-8-deploy-to-production-manual--approved-pipeline","content":"It uses the same migration and review process without the agent ever touching the production credentials. You can again verify the details on your production database."},"3414":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-100","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-8-deploy-to-production-manual--approved-pipeline","content":"Before:"},"3415":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-101","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#step-8-deploy-to-production-manual--approved-pipeline","content":"After:"},"3416":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-102","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#how-this-maps-to-real-production-setups","content":"In the demo above, we used two local Postgres databases (shop_sandbox and shop_validate) to illustrate isolation."},"3417":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-103","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#how-this-maps-to-real-production-setups","content":"In real systems, this isolation usually already exists in production, staging, and development database environments. Modern database platforms make it straightforward to create and manage these environments."},"3418":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-104","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#how-this-maps-to-real-production-setups","content":"For example, Managed Postgres (RDS, Cloud SQL, Neon, Supabase) has read replicas, cloned databases, and point-in-time snapshots that are restored into new instances. Data warehouses have schema-level clones (Snowflake, BigQuery) and masked production extracts."},"3419":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-105","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#how-this-maps-to-real-production-setups","content":"As a user, all you need to do is route the agent to the correct tier depending on the operation you intend to perform."},"3420":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-106","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#conclusion","content":"In this tutorial, we displayed why tool-level restrictions are not enough and how agents can still bypass read-only controls if they have any execution surface."},"3421":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-107","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#conclusion","content":"The safest approach is to separate reasoning from execution:"},"3422":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-108","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#conclusion","content":"Tier 1: Read-only access via narrow tools"},"3423":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-109","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#conclusion","content":"Tier 2: Writable clones + validated migration scripts"},"3424":{"id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi-110","page_id":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/secure-db-access-in-pochi#conclusion","content":"This gives agents useful autonomy while keeping your production systems protected."},"3425":{"id":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server","page_id":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server","type":"page","content":"Build a Custom MCP Server to Query Supabase","url":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server"},"3426":{"id":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server-0","page_id":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server","type":"text","url":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server","content":"Build a custom MCP server in Pochi that lets you run natural language SQL queries on your Supabase database."},"3427":{"id":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server-1","page_id":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server#build-a-custom-mcp-server-to-query-supabase","content":"Build a Custom MCP Server to Query Supabase"},"3428":{"id":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server-2","page_id":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites"},"3429":{"id":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server-3","page_id":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server#what-is-mcp-model-context-protocol","content":"What is MCP (Model Context Protocol)?"},"3430":{"id":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server-4","page_id":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server#getting-started-how-to-build-the-mcp-server","content":"Getting Started: How to Build the MCP Server"},"3431":{"id":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server-5","page_id":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server#step-1-setup-your-vs-code-project","content":"Step 1: Setup your VS Code project"},"3432":{"id":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server-6","page_id":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server#create-a-env-file","content":"Create a .env file"},"3433":{"id":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server-7","page_id":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server#step-2-create-your-supabase-database","content":"Step 2: Create your Supabase Database"},"3434":{"id":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server-8","page_id":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server#step-3-prompt-pochi-to-build-out-the-mcp-server--supabase-client","content":"Step 3: Prompt Pochi to build out the MCP server & Supabase Client"},"3435":{"id":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server-9","page_id":"/tutorials/supabase-mcp-server","type":"heading","url":"/tutorials/supab