hi's Parallel Agents for concurrent development - learn best practices through a hands-on project."],[2348,"A shell is a general-purpose programming environment. Once exposed, safety boundaries become undefined."],[3040,"A shell is a general-purpose programming environment. Once exposed, safety boundaries become undefined."],[3240,"A single AI agent completes task A → waits → then task B → waits → then task C. Three 15-minute tasks executed sequentially would take 45 minutes in total. In software development, for example, one agent builds the backend API → then the frontend → then writes tests."],[921,"A small but solid update this week. Pochi now ignores large dependency directories like node_modules when building the file context for a task, even if the repository doesn’t define a .gitignore. We also fixed a few edge cases that could cause checkpointing to hang."],[2186,"A small but solid update this week. Pochi now ignores large dependency directories like node_modules when building the file context for a task, even if the repository doesn’t define a .gitignore. We also fixed a few edge cases that could cause checkpointing to hang."],[703,"A small step closer to a more transparent, predictable coding agent."],[2628,"A small step closer to a more transparent, predictable coding agent."],[2520,"A speculated prediction remains valid as long as the user is essentially still typing into the suggestion and the surrounding context hasn't changed."],[2980,"A speculated prediction remains valid as long as the user is essentially still typing into the suggestion and the surrounding context hasn't changed."],[122,"A tool declared without parentheses (e.g., readFile) has no restrictions. Use one declaration per rule — commas inside a specifier are not supported; add separate entries for multiple rules."],[3173,"A Visual Conversation for Complex Tasks"],[3255,"A well-structured design document is crucial when working with parallel agents. It serves as the single source of truth that all agents will reference to understand the project requirements, architecture, and their specific responsibilities."],[3099,"A. Set Your Hotkey\nChoose a shortcut that does not conflict with other apps. Handy supports both push-to-talk and toggle behaviors. Enable Push to Talk if you want to hold the shortcut while speaking; otherwise, use the default press-to-start, press-again-to-stop mode."],[422,"Accept the current suggestion"],[468,"Access the Pochi chat panel via the Activity Bar icon or shortcut (macOS: Cmd+L, Win/Linux: Ctrl+L). This is your main interface for interacting with Pochi. Note: An active workspace (i.e., an open folder) is required to use the chat."],[1343,"Across a typical month of publishing, this reduces roughly 8 hours of manual work to under 10 minutes, removing a significant amount of repetitive effort from our workflow."],[2132,"Across a typical month of publishing, this reduces roughly 8 hours of manual work to under 10 minutes, removing a significant amount of repetitive effort from our workflow."],[420,"Action"],[3108,"Activate Handy: Click inside Pochi's input box, then use the shortcut you configured for Handy. Handy shows an on-screen indicator when it is listening."],[363,"Activating Skills"],[227,"Add project-specific MCP servers"],[295,"Add tasks to a queue while Pochi is busy, ensuring a non-blocking experience."],[3390,"Add the new server to config.jsonc:"],[304,"Add, view, and manage line-level comments directly on the diff code"],[617,"Added Linux ARM64 Release: Pochi is now available for Linux ARM64 systems, improving compatibility for developers running on Raspberry Pi or ARM-based environments. #543"],[2738,"Added Linux ARM64 Release: Pochi is now available for Linux ARM64 systems, improving compatibility for developers running on Raspberry Pi or ARM-based environments. #543"],[1373,"Additional context from other files (optional): e.g., functions/type declarations that help understand the current file"],[2590,"Addi