upport in CLI: The Pochi CLI can now run browser-powered tasks.\nPreviously, browser sessions were managed inside the VS Code extension only. That meant any task requiring a live browser - navigating websites, extracting content, interacting with pages, etc wasn’t supported in the CLI."],[1157,"Browser Agent with Viewport Size: Browser Agent sessions now let you pick a viewport size before running. Four presets: Large Desktop (1280×720), Small Desktop (900×600), Portrait (768×1024), and Mobile (360×640), selectable from a new dropdown in Browser Agent Settings. The recording scales to match."],[1979,"Browser Agent with Viewport Size: Browser Agent sessions now let you pick a viewport size before running. Four presets: Large Desktop (1280×720), Small Desktop (900×600), Portrait (768×1024), and Mobile (360×640), selectable from a new dropdown in Browser Agent Settings. The recording scales to match."],[1112,"Browser Recording Codec and Canvas: Browser recordings no longer fail on platforms where the hard-coded H.264 codec isn't available — the recorder now detects a supported codec at runtime. Frames are also rendered to a consistent 854×480 canvas with letterboxing, fixing distorted or broken recordings from variable source dimensions. #1535, #1537"],[2027,"Browser Recording Codec and Canvas: Browser recordings no longer fail on platforms where the hard-coded H.264 codec isn't available — the recorder now detects a supported codec at runtime. Frames are also rendered to a consistent 854×480 canvas with letterboxing, fixing distorted or broken recordings from variable source dimensions. #1535, #1537"],[3193,"Browser/Environment Dependencies: Components with direct dependencies on browser-specific features like XTerm.js, VS Code APIs, and file system interactions."],[982,"Bug fixes"],[2152,"Bug fixes"],[522,"Bug fixes 🐛"],[541,"Bug fixes 🐛"],[1849,"Bug fixes 🐛"],[1857,"Bug fixes 🐛"],[490,"Bug Fixes 🐛"],[501,"Bug Fixes 🐛"],[1864,"Bug Fixes 🐛"],[1871,"Bug Fixes 🐛"],[3426